A||N||6||stimpy||Installation question for Pioneer DEH-77DH owners.||||5||
Z||000000||stimpy||02-23-2001||02:14 PM||||My CD player is due to be delivered on February 28th, and I can't wait to get it installed. My question is, where do I splice the wire for the Alarm+ feature into the door pin wire? Do I need to run a line to each door pin, or is there a central location I can tap into? Thanks in advance for the help.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||02-23-2001||02:29 PM||||You can tap into any pin switch. They are all the same circuit. Just hook to 1 of them and your ready to go. If you hook to driver side the passenger door will also set it off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||02-23-2001||02:32 PM||||Dayum. that was quick! Thanks for lookin out, Oreif!||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||02-23-2001||07:02 PM||||Oh yeah, one more thing. What color is that wire and is there somewhere easy to tap into it without pulling apart the interior?||||reg||5
Z||000004||cifc||02-23-2001||09:40 PM||||The wire is white.  The easiest place to get it is at the under dash lights.<BR>--Jason||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||02-23-2001||09:48 PM||||The door switch wire is white. You can access it just above the carpet on the left side under the dash. Also if your going to add keyless entry, The wires are dark blue and light blue. (I don't remember which one is lock and unlock)If you hold a meter on one of them you should see 12V when the button (lock or unlock) is pressed. To splice into the wire, Use an Xacto knife and cut the sleeving off. Then insert the alarm wire thru the strands of the factory, Solder and then wrap with electrical tape. If you cut the wire, use sleeving.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||02-24-2001||01:47 AM||||I spliced into the wire on the passenger side, right by the bulb.  Very easy, and you can tuck the wire up under the dash.||||reg||1
